WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.730
<i>Students have no money.</i>

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:06.800
<i>The money we receive at New Year's...</i>

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.570
<i>disappears with the 
melting winter snow...</i>

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:12.380
<i>and our meager daily 
allowance whittles down to zero...</i>

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:16.640
<i>from the moment it's put into our hands.</i>

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.810
Are you stupid?!

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.500
You paid 100 yen for tea?!

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.210
Who cares what I buy?

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:33.790
If you're gonna buy anything, 
you should get juice like normal people.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:34.600
Right?

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.820
What a waste of money.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:41.980
Instead of spending money on that, 
you could have had some at home for free.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:47.510
I bet Kaname thinks he 
can even buy love with his money.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:50.800
I bet he thinks there's 
nothing he can't buy.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:51.830
Huh?

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:55.360
Haven't we had this conversation before?

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:00.120
This is what you call "smart shopping."

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:03.820
Look. Lots of different fruits in one carton...

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:05.370
Mix juice!

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:09.420
Who cares what I buy with my own money?

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.500
It doesn't affect you.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:16.090
You're so full of yourself, Kaname-kun.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:19.110
I can't even afford juice.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:22.490
Huh? Yuki-kun, aren't you 
going to buy some juice?

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:25.760
Yuki's broke for the moment.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:28.270
What am I going to do?

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:32.020
I won't be able to buy First Fantasy.

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:34.470
It comes out next week.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:40.440
Yuki-kun.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.740
Why don't you get a part time job?

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:45.540
A what?

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:47.690
A job?

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:10.660
A job?

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:11.620
Yes.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.130
For Kaname?

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:15.680
For you.

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:18.440
You want <i>me</i> to work?

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:21.870
We're almost third years now.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:23.140
This might be your last chance

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:26.570
to get a job before you become 
too busy with entrance exams.

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.890
A job's a great idea! 
You should do it, Yukki.

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:33.510
No, forget it.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.230
I'm no good with customers.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:38.030
Dealing with customers is a piece of cake!

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.820
All you have to do is smile.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.600
Welcome.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:43.380
How many in your party?

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:44.830
Just like that, right?

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:47.540
Table for one?

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:51.080
I see. Nobody to eat with, huh?

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:53.900
Like that, you mean?

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.830
You're not supposed to laugh about it.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.630
I wonder what kind of 
job would fit Yuki-kun.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.990
Wait, I didn't say I was gonna—

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:04.200
Okay, okay!

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.780
Let's have a meeting to 
determine Yukki's job.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:11.030
I think he'd do well in a bookstore.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:13.250
Yuki-kun likes manga.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:24.490
Well, I guess it'd be nice to read 
all the new magazines for free.

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:28.500
Employees can't just stand there and 
read their store's merchandise.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.520
How about sitting instead?

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:33.590
It's not about <i>how</i> you read it.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:37.200
I bet they have lots 
of cute little picture books.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.780
Yeah, like "Shun-chan in Wonderland."

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.760
I can see that.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:48.330
Don't part-time jobs make 
you think of fast food?

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:49.680
No, no.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.770
This guy wouldn't earn 
a dime for his smile.

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:55.990
He won't even smile for money.

00:04:55.990 --> 00:05:01.850
Hey, I'd smile if I knew someone
 was going to pay me for it.

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.520
Your smile is so shady.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:09.450
That's just not you, Yukki.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:12.040
You should do something like...

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:19.790
Everyone else here is just a customer.

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.350
But you're different.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:24.180
Oh, my.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:25.720
Here, have these.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.800
He's gotta become a host.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.310
Hey, lady killer.

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:32.960
A-A night worker?

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:35.530
Two million yen a night is 
tough to argue with.

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:37.770
Two million?

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:41.220
That's more money than 
I can even make sense of.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:45.380
Yeah, having just a thousand yen 
makes you feel rich.

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:49.140
Hey, don't you guys want 
to make some money?!

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:51.680
High schoolers can't do jobs like that.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:55.700
Delivering newspapers.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:57.030
That's it.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:06:00.650
Your first job should 
be delivering newspapers.

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:03.860
But I want to sleep in as late as I can.

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:05.310
No, no.

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:07.350
He's gotta be a host of the night.

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:08.900
Right, Yukki?

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:12.710
I'd rather just sleep at night.

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:15.100
Never mind working, do you 
even want to be alive?

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:17.730
It's fine, really.

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:19.610
I won't work.

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:24.050
But Yuki, if you don't find work, 
you can't buy your game.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:25.380
Are you okay with that?

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:27.890
That's right, Yukki.

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:30.240
Yuki-kun, just give it a go.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.250
Okay?

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:37.500
Fine.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:44.560
Time to work for my game.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:46.360
Kaname, I mean.

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:49.010
I told you, <i>you're</i> the 
one who has to work.

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:56.200
That's how 17-year-old Asaba Yuki 
got the first job of his life.

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:02.550
I'm going to eat until I burst today!

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:04.640
Wanna start at one end of the 
menu and go through it all?

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:05.550
Yes, let's do it.

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:07.560
Thank you for waiting.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:09.880
May I take your order?

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:11.450
I'd like the hamburger <i>demi-glace</i>,

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:14.090
the seafood curry, the pudding 
parfait, and a milk tea.

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:17.540
I'd like the steak, the doria, the 
cheesecake, and a royal milk tea.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:21.670
The royal milk tea comes iced or hot.

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:23.670
Which would you prefer?

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:26.170
Oh, actually...

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:31.400
Instead of all that, can we 
just get two black coffees?

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.700
You can get your coffees at the drink bar.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:35.260
Will that be all right?

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:37.070
Uh, yes.

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:38.410
Very well.

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:42.660
The drink bar is over there. Enjoy.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:47.970
Who was that?!

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:49.440
He's so hot.

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:51.800
Ah, Asaba-kun.

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:55.950
Take this special mix juice 
to the customers at A-6.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:56.800
Okay.

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:00.450
I'm tired.

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:04.260
I figured that because there'd 
be fewer customers on a weekday,

00:08:04.260 --> 00:08:06.040
I'd have more free time.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:06.900
Excuse me.

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:07.920
Can I get some water?

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:10.010
Why is it so busy?

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:08.860
Excuse me.

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:10.010
Can I get some here, too?

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:10.960
Excuse me, waiter.

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:14.350
Thank you for waiting.

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:16.470
Here's your special mix juice...

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:20.340
You're working hard, Yukki-kun.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.890
What are you all doing here?

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:24.390
What are we doing?

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:26.550
We were wondering how you were doing,

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:28.830
so we came to see for ourselves.

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:32.320
You guys are terrible.

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:34.410
How's work?

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.770
I might quit.

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:38.410
It's hard.

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:41.630
Hold up. It's still your first day.

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:45.910
You give up way too easily.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:50.250
We saw you taking orders.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:54.410
I thought you'd be washing 
dishes in the back.

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:59.700
Well, they said I'd be working 
in back when I was interviewed,

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:03.590
but my boss told me to 
work the floor today.

00:09:03.590 --> 00:09:07.410
Hey, what's your boss 
like? Is she pretty?

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:08.870
There you go again.

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:11.450
No, not even close...

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:12.360
Ow.

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:18.520
Asaba, why are you taking a break?

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:21.090
Boss.

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:25.190
Um, Boss...

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:26.210
What?

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:31.250
I'm supposed to be a dishwasher.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.270
What are you, stupid?

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:36.880
With your looks, you should 
be working the floor.

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:41.720
You're more of a gang
 leader than a boss.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:42.710
What?

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:44.350
Nothing.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:48.290
Are you guys Asaba's friends?

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:50.000
Have you eaten already?

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:54.320
I-I'm sorry. We don't 
have very much money.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:56.250
We'll probably only order drinks.

00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:58.580
Sorry for being such bad customers.

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:00.430
What are you apologizing for?

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:03.060
Order whatever you want.

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:05.410
In here, the customers are gods.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:06.500
What?

00:10:08.610 --> 00:10:10.500
Take your time.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.980
My boss is scary.

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:18.240
Y-Your boss is scary. He's terrifying.

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:20.090
The godfather.

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:24.910
He seems like a pretty 
dependable boss to me.

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:28.480
Maybe he'll be able to make Yuki...

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:29.660
Welcome.

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:32.920
Yukki, work hard.

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:35.210
Work hard?

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:38.400
You guys are casually ordering 
drinks while I'm working.

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:40.070
Your encouragement 
doesn't mean anything.

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:43.070
Is this on the house, Yukki?

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:45.180
What?

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:49.210
No, you ordered that.

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:52.670
You must really love mix juice.

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:53.630
What?

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:57.630
We haven't ordered anything yet.

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:00.240
What? Then, this is...

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:01.680
This is ridiculous.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:05.070
How long does it take to 
make a single mix juice?

00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:06.930
It's still not ready yet?

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:11.190
Maybe he accidentally took 
it to another table.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:13.250
You can't be serious.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:20.340
Hey!

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:22.160
This isn't ours!

00:11:23.340 --> 00:11:26.030
Why did you have to drink it, Chizuru?

00:11:26.030 --> 00:11:29.790
Why did <i>you</i> bring it to us?

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:34.850
Y-You should apologize to your boss,

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:38.550
and make those customers a new mix juice.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:40.440
I can't do that.

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:43.740
If the boss finds out, he'll dock my pay.

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:46.330
That's right. If we're not careful...

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:49.560
What? You drank someone else's juice?

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:52.200
He'll kill us!

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:55.380
You only care about yourselves.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:56.660
But...

00:11:56.660 --> 00:11:58.220
What are we gonna do?

00:11:58.220 --> 00:11:59.490
I know.

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:02.150
Yuki-kun, you have an idea?

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:04.100
I'm going back to work.

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:08.160
Hold on! Don't you dare run from this!

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.660
I'm not.

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:13.640
If I don't stand out on the floor, 
I'll look even more suspicious.

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:17.420
But weren't you just heading 
towards the locker room?

00:12:17.810 --> 00:12:21.830
I'll look suspicious if I walk 
around outside in these clothes.

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:23.180
I have to go change.

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:26.930
You were going home, weren't you?

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:32.420
Okay, okay. Fine.

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:36.000
Let's go secretly prepare 
another mix juice.

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:37.730
Yuta-kun.

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:39.490
Huh? What?

00:12:57.060 --> 00:12:58.790
Stop it, Sacchan.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:00.830
Don't kick your feet like that.

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:03.140
Mind your manners when you're eating.

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:07.740
See?

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:14.020
What cute shoes.

00:13:15.530 --> 00:13:18.610
You should wear them so 
you don't lose them.

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:25.380
Th-Thank you.

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:26.510
Not at all.

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:34.450
Yuta-kun's so cool.

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:36.280
Yutan, looking good.

00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:40.230
He looks just like me in those clothes.

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:42.070
No, he doesn't.

00:13:42.070 --> 00:13:44.420
His work ethic's nothing like yours.

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:48.970
Okay, while Yuta's 
pretending to be me,

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:52.470
let's prepare that mix juice.

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:55.320
Us? What are you...

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:56.920
I see.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:59.650
You can make a mix juice 
at the drink bar.

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:03.070
But it's called a special mix juice...

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:05.570
because there's something
 special in it, right?

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:07.830
Won't they find out?

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:11.450
They might,

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:17.130
but I get the feeling they'll be nice about it,

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:20.210
instead of getting mad.

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:25.660
Yuki-kun, you have so much 
faith in your customers.

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:26.920
Look.

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:30.420
How does it take this long 
to make a mix juice?

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:32.400
She kinda looks like Anpanda.

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:32.010
I don't believe this.

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:34.050
This is infuriating.

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:36.320
I think she might be surprisingly nice.

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:39.980
She's gonna be pissed.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:41.690
He was so hot.

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:42.440
Thank you very much.

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:42.930
What do you want to go eat now?

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:44.120
Steak.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:53.790
Hurry up.

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:55.740
Excuse me.

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:57.510
Yes, I'll be right there.

00:15:06.330 --> 00:15:07.790
This isn't bad.

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:09.930
It's good. It's pretty good.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:12.880
Let's see if we can get even 
closer to the real thing.

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:15.970
Let's try to bring out the 
thickness of the juice...

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:19.040
with some corn starch!

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:22.220
That'll only turn it into mapo tofu.

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:24.370
Kaname-kun, Chizuru-kun.

00:15:24.370 --> 00:15:26.110
I found some good ingredients.

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:28.740
Try using this.

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:30.760
These smell like weeds.

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:35.730
Cafes usually garnish their 
drinks with some kind of plant.

00:15:35.730 --> 00:15:38.210
Where did you get this?

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:42.250
I can't wait much longer.

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:45.400
Don't actually put grass in here.

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:48.510
This isn't garnish, it's a weed.

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:53.370
I see. They say you taste 
with your eyes first.

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:54.760
You can't taste this!

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:58.870
Honestly... Hey, Shun. Say something.

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:02.600
Don't add more!

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:06.190
But, isn't it cute like a tropical juice?

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:09.400
What are you guys doing?

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:10.770
You can't serve this to anyone.

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:11.650
So mean.

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:13.690
You're oppressing art.

00:16:13.690 --> 00:16:15.320
How is this art?

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:17.590
Oh, crap!

00:16:16.730 --> 00:16:19.110
Excuse me, Manager.

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:19.950
She's calling the boss over!

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:24.050
It's the boss!

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:27.490
Wh-What are we going to do?

00:16:27.490 --> 00:16:29.460
We don't have time to make a new one.

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:31.410
Calm down, Shun-chan.

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:34.870
I'll go buy some mix juice from school.

00:16:35.900 --> 00:16:37.900
Chizuru, calm down.

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:42.060
Hey, isn't there any way to do 
this besides the drink bar?

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:46.230
Let's do this.

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:49.960
I'll go to the kitchen and get 
a blender and some ingredients.

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:51.570
We should've done that 
in the first place!

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:57.090
How long are you going to make 
us wait for a mix juice?

00:16:57.090 --> 00:16:58.950
I'm terribly sorry.

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:01.210
I'll go get you one immediately.

00:17:01.190 --> 00:17:04.910
That won't be necessary! 
Let's go, Kubota-san!

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:06.180
Please wait.

00:17:06.180 --> 00:17:07.920
Excuse me.

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:11.580
Here's your special mix juice.

00:17:14.060 --> 00:17:16.800
I'm sorry. Watch your feet.

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:18.910
Hey! What are you doing?

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:24.250
I wanted to give our customers 
freshly-made juice.

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:25.310
What?

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:32.500
You've already got a complaint 
on your first day.

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:34.110
I'm docking your pay 
as of your next shift—

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:35.170
Boss.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:40.490
I'm sorry. This is Yuki-kun's first job.

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:43.390
I'm sorry for all the 
trouble he's caused today.

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:48.750
But he'll work even harder from now on.

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:51.970
Could you please wait 
to cut his pay until...

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:54.580
you see how he performs in the future?

00:17:58.500 --> 00:17:59.980
Please.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:11.070
W-Well, if you insist.

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:13.650
Y-Yeah.

00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:23.100
Here we go.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:35.670
Hey, wai—

00:18:56.900 --> 00:19:01.700
Dry cleaning the customer's 
clothes: 3,900 yen.

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:07.690
The mix juice you drank and then 
splattered from the blender: 840 yen.

00:19:07.690 --> 00:19:12.210
That's 4,740 yen I'm 
deducting from your pay.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:18.050
And you're fired.

00:19:20.860 --> 00:19:23.720
Naturally, after that, you have no pay left.

00:19:24.820 --> 00:19:27.180
Isn't there at least a 
few hundred yen left...

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:28.730
after all those deductions?

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:31.110
No, there isn't.

00:19:31.110 --> 00:19:33.480
And even if there was 
anything left, I'd give it...

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:35.850
to your brother, not you.

00:19:36.930 --> 00:19:41.240
Um, I'm sorry for switching 
places with him.

00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:45.600
You were a worthless employee.

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:48.150
You couldn't even smile 
for the customers.

00:19:48.150 --> 00:19:49.750
If you look for work again,

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:53.890
find something better suited to you.

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:57.640
I think there's plenty of jobs out 
there that you're suited for...

00:19:57.640 --> 00:19:59.720
more than running a family restaurant, too.

00:20:02.450 --> 00:20:06.950
You can think of this as an 
expensive learning experience.

00:20:14.280 --> 00:20:18.540
Earning money isn't easy, Asaba-kun.

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:29.080
Even high school kids get fired 
without a second thought these days.

00:20:29.520 --> 00:20:33.790
That's not why he got fired.

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:37.780
Yuki-kun, failure breeds success.

00:20:37.780 --> 00:20:41.060
I'm sure this will help 
you in the future.

00:20:41.060 --> 00:20:44.260
I won't be getting another 
job for a while.

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:46.950
Well, it wasn't all bad.

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:49.360
You earned some experience points.

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:53.730
I'd rather have money 
than experience points.

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:57.270
<i>Students have no money.</i>

00:20:57.840 --> 00:21:01.830
<i>My first job disappeared in my boss' rage.</i>

00:21:02.370 --> 00:21:05.080
<i>Because I received no pay,</i>

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:08.060
<i>the game I wanted slipped 
even further from my grasp.</i>

00:21:08.960 --> 00:21:10.040
Excuse me.

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:17.580
Are you the person who picked 
up my shoe in the restaurant?

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:18.470
What?

00:21:18.470 --> 00:21:20.260
It <i>is</i> you.

00:21:22.030 --> 00:21:26.090
I felt like I was Cinderella.

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:27.410
Huh?

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:30.350
Because... because...

00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:34.850
You were so wonderful, like a prince.

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:37.350
What? A prince?

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:39.860
I don't know what you're...

00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:39.860
Huh? Yukki...

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:41.360
Thank you.

00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:46.410
Sacchan, what are you doing?

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:48.160
Let's go.

00:21:55.250 --> 00:22:00.130
Yukki-san, did she just kiss you?

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:01.910
No.

00:22:01.910 --> 00:22:04.430
No, no. I know she did.

00:22:04.430 --> 00:22:05.840
No, she didn't.

00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:09.100
She totally did.

00:22:09.100 --> 00:22:10.690
No, she didn't.

00:22:11.920 --> 00:22:14.840
Yukki, you just lost your kiss virginity.

00:22:15.830 --> 00:22:17.760
Good going, man.

00:22:17.760 --> 00:22:21.060
You got the best reward 
a man could ask for.

00:22:21.060 --> 00:22:22.820
She didn't kiss me.

00:22:22.820 --> 00:22:26.060
Yuki, I'll buy you some lemon squash.

00:22:26.060 --> 00:22:27.910
Then, it'll taste like lemons.

00:22:27.910 --> 00:22:29.560
She didn't kiss me.

00:22:32.100 --> 00:22:35.110
Isn't work fun, Yukki?

00:24:17.290 --> 00:24:19.350
The next episode is "Cherry."
